<title>BRAZIL: Brazil March pulp exports up 27 pct on 1996 - Abecel.</title>
<headline>Brazil March pulp exports up 27 pct on 1996 - Abecel.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian pulp exports reached a record 242,000 tonnes in March, up 27 percent from the same month last year, the Brazilian Pulp Exporters' Association (Abecel) said in a statement.</p>
<p>In the first quarter of this year, Brazil has now exported 588,000 tonnes, up 32 percent on the corresponding period in 1996, it added.</p>
<p>Asia was the main destination for Brazilian pulp during January to March, importing 225,000 tonnes, a growth of 51 percent on last year.</p>
<p>Within the region, China and Indonesia both imported 30,000 tonnes each.</p>
<p>Very close behind was Europe which imported 223,000 tonnes, up 64 percent from last year.</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
